  "description": "In collaboration with the School of Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences, the School of Graduate and Continuing Studies offers a BA in human services. Grounded in a Christian perspective, this interdisciplinary major combines theory and skills to prepare students for serving in their communities with cultural humility, interpersonal skills, and strong ethical conduct. Students examine societal tensions and causes of injustice while learning about human behavior, with a focus on facilitating positive change. In addition to the requirements of the major, students also must satisfy the requirements of the degree-completion Core curriculum.",
